# Example crontab lines for running the world locally on your Pro/Max subscription.
# Edit the path, then install with: crontab -e  (paste these lines in)

# Simulate: free, no LLM call - safe to run often. Every 15 minutes here.
*/15 * * * * cd /path/to/self-evolving-world && /usr/bin/python3 driver.py simulate >> logs/simulate.log 2>&1

# Evolve: calls Claude via your Pro subscription (config.py, WORLD_BACKEND=cli
# by default). Keep this infrequent - once a day is the default budget in
# state/budget.json. Pick a quiet time when you're not also using Claude Code
# for your own work, since they share the same usage pool.
0 3 * * * cd /path/to/self-evolving-world && /usr/bin/python3 driver.py evolve >> logs/evolve.log 2>&1

# Note: `claude` must already be authenticated (`claude login`) under the same
# user account that cron runs as. Test with `crontab -l` and a manual
# `python3 driver.py evolve` run first before trusting the schedule.
